minimalReproduction.edit:
ONE contiguous replacement. ',
    "theEnumerationIsAGateToo": <value>
  },' becomes '
  },
  "thePrimitive/theEnumerationIsAGateToo": <value>,' -- the same string value, relocated from a child of thePrimitive to the next sibling key of thePrimitive at the document root, named with the literal text of its old path. Nothing else changes. The position matters as much as the name: document_skeleton is an ORDERED list, and inserting the relocated node immediately after its own top-level ancestor preserves the walk order too, which is why the digest is byte-identical rather than merely equal as a set.
